SUMMARY:Special Event: Joey Dardano
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 1510 SE 9th Ave\, Portland
DESCRIPTION:Joey Dardano is an actor\, comedian\, singer and writer based o
 ut of Brooklyn. Growing up in a Cuban/Italian family in South Florida\, he 
 attended theatre programs at prestigious middle and high schools\, crooning
  ballads and landing double pirouettes (sometimes). He is trained at Stella
  Adler and The New School for Dramatic Arts\, and has studied voice under A
 aron Hagan (Ariana Grande\, Meghan Trainor) since he was 18.\n\nJoey is a f
 eatured cast member on Wild ‘N Out on VH1\, starred in Joe Picozzi’s 
 “My Kind of People” which won The Russo Bros’ Italian Filmmaker Forum
 \, and had a major supporting role in Jonah Feingold’s rom-com\, “31 Ca
 ndles”. He’ll next be seen recurring in Season 2 of FX’s hit show “
 Adults".\n\nHe stars in the digital series "The Method with Joey Dardano" w
 hich he created alongside Stapleview and The Laugh Factory. In April 2026\,
  he debuted a new podcast with Sonoro / iHeartMedia called “Help From a H
 ypocrite".\n\nJoey is currently touring the country and world as a standup 
 and spent two years as a member of the touring cast of the hit live comedy 
 extravaganza STAMPTOWN.\n\nCouple's Package includes:\n\n- 2 premium seats\
 n- $90 food & beverage credit ($45 per person)\n- Gratuity\n- Ticket Protec
 tion\n\nManagement reserves the right to prevent customers from entering th
 e facility who they deem disruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore in
 fo: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/special-event-joey-dardano/
